WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:11.688
Millions of people manage type 1 diabetes, day after day. They depend on insulin and other essential supplies. Having them when they are needed matters.

00:00:12.168 --> 00:00:25.704
Even with careful planning, sometimes a supply runs low. People reach out to family, friends, and local T1D groups. That support matters, but it does not reach everyone.

00:00:26.184 --> 00:00:40.512
This idea came from a real personal experience. That is why VoiceOfT1D created this web exchange: to help more people find each other, anywhere in the world. A mobile app is a future goal.

00:00:40.992 --> 00:00:46.752
First, sign in if you already have an account, or select Register to create one.

00:00:47.232 --> 00:00:54.216
To share an item, choose Offer Supplies. If prompted, sign in to continue.

00:00:54.696 --> 00:01:00.888
Jordan adds the item type, condition, and location, then chooses how to share it.

00:01:01.368 --> 00:01:06.384
Need something? Choose Register Need to let the community know.

00:01:06.864 --> 00:01:14.544
Maya registers the supply she needs and adds her city or ZIP code. No exact address is needed.

00:01:15.024 --> 00:01:22.272
She reviews approximate matches. Check again reruns the search for newly available offers.

00:01:22.752 --> 00:01:31.272
Maya asks to connect. Jordan can approve or decline, and her contact details stay private while he decides.

00:01:31.752 --> 00:01:38.616
Jordan approves. Now they can share contact details and talk through what works for them.

00:01:39.096 --> 00:01:52.584
And that's the heart of this exchange. Insulin, test strips, CGM or pump supplies, and more. When something runs low, people can find each other and offer a hand.
